1
00:00:35,454 --> 00:00:45,934
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

2
00:02:04,531 --> 00:02:08,531
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:51,103
Hang on, Dervish.

4
00:02:57,867 --> 00:02:59,227
He is bleeding so badly.

5
00:02:59,227 --> 00:03:00,667
Can we really save him?

6
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:03,087
As long as we try, Allah will heal him.

7
00:03:03,087 --> 00:03:04,107
Come on. Hurry up.

8
00:03:12,741 --> 00:03:13,501
Alişar!

9
00:03:16,546 --> 00:03:17,306
Ya Allah!

10
00:03:26,448 --> 00:03:27,328
Alişar!

11
00:03:39,316 --> 00:03:40,086
Alişar!

12
00:03:40,529 --> 00:03:41,699
Alişar Bey!

13
00:03:42,679 --> 00:03:44,049
Open the gates now!

14
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,960
They are keep yelling outside.

15
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,190
Alişar!

16
00:03:48,577 --> 00:03:49,797
What are we waiting for?

17
00:03:50,215 --> 00:03:51,825
Let’s go out and fight!

18
00:03:53,289 --> 00:03:56,129
Nobody will listen to us if we don’t
shut them up now.

19
00:03:57,213 --> 00:03:58,323
We will.

20
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,250
We will cut...

21
00:04:00,824 --> 00:04:01,944
...first their voice...

22
00:04:02,195 --> 00:04:03,825
...then their head!

23
00:04:09,076 --> 00:04:11,536
May every bite you took from my bowl be
illicit…

24
00:04:12,230 --> 00:04:15,260
…if you don’t make a pond of blood out
there!

25
00:04:17,909 --> 00:04:18,629
Alişar!

26
00:04:19,815 --> 00:04:21,185
Open the gates!

27
00:05:02,227 --> 00:05:03,427
Alişar!

28
00:05:10,592 --> 00:05:13,592
You are going to pay for knocking on
my door like this, Gündüz.

29
00:05:13,719 --> 00:05:15,319
We are not here to pay something.

30
00:05:15,712 --> 00:05:17,422
We are here to shed blood!

31
00:05:21,219 --> 00:05:22,989
You once seized my title by force.

32
00:05:24,131 --> 00:05:27,111
My nephew, are you going to seize my life
now?

33
00:05:27,965 --> 00:05:29,315
We pulled your strings...

34
00:05:29,315 --> 00:05:31,897
...before you started a bloody rebellion
at our Tent.

35
00:05:31,897 --> 00:05:33,117
We spoiled your game.

36
00:05:34,482 --> 00:05:35,972
Don’t you ever talk, uncle!

37
00:05:37,751 --> 00:05:40,821
What are you talking about, Gündüz?

38
00:05:43,638 --> 00:05:44,608
Soldiers!

39
00:05:45,263 --> 00:05:46,743
Arms down!

40
00:05:56,898 --> 00:06:00,668
If Dündar Bey had really done something
like that…

41
00:06:01,099 --> 00:06:03,619
…he would have been killed by me
already, Gündüz.

42
00:06:04,978 --> 00:06:06,628
You should tell this to yourself…

43
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,060
…not me.

44
00:06:12,265 --> 00:06:14,495
Every game he played...

45
00:06:15,025 --> 00:06:17,585
...has brought shame upon our Tent.

46
00:06:18,542 --> 00:06:19,932
As well as lies…

47
00:06:20,691 --> 00:06:21,711
…and blood!

48
00:06:22,454 --> 00:06:25,144
Do you think you left me any other
choice...

49
00:06:25,144 --> 00:06:27,322
...to get what is rightfully mine?

50
00:06:27,322 --> 00:06:30,112
Do you think I am stupid?

51
00:06:30,112 --> 00:06:31,692
You are a fool, Dündar!

52
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:36,140
You are stupid enough to let your
daughter marry...

53
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:37,830
...the murderer of your own son!

54
00:06:42,459 --> 00:06:43,819
The murderer of your son!

55
00:07:18,016 --> 00:07:19,646
In the name of Allah.

56
00:07:20,295 --> 00:07:22,325
My Sheikh, try not to tire yourself.

57
00:07:22,325 --> 00:07:23,975
Please get some rest.

58
00:07:24,446 --> 00:07:26,846
Working is a duty for all, my Zulfiqar.

59
00:07:27,621 --> 00:07:32,571
Serving in the way of Allah is the most
sacred blessing reserved to men.

60
00:07:46,631 --> 00:07:47,771
My Sheikh!

61
00:07:55,488 --> 00:07:56,978
I hope everything is okay.

62
00:07:56,978 --> 00:07:58,438
May Allah be with us.

63
00:08:20,535 --> 00:08:21,485
Osman!

64
00:08:21,565 --> 00:08:22,325
Osman!

65
00:08:22,962 --> 00:08:23,882
-My Osman!
-Osman!

66
00:08:23,975 --> 00:08:25,085
-Run!
-Osman!

67
00:08:28,317 --> 00:08:29,197
Osman!?

68
00:08:30,989 --> 00:08:32,479
Osman!

69
00:08:37,491 --> 00:08:39,411
My Osman! Who did this to you?

70
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:45,424
My Allah, don't make me feel this pain.

71
00:08:47,786 --> 00:08:48,926
My Osman!

72
00:08:51,799 --> 00:08:53,489
Thanks to Allah, he is still alive.

73
00:08:53,489 --> 00:08:54,999
Build the fire immediately!

74
00:09:09,835 --> 00:09:11,225
Come on, faster!

75
00:09:11,225 --> 00:09:12,705
Who did this to you?

76
00:09:13,365 --> 00:09:14,325
My Osman!

77
00:09:14,325 --> 00:09:15,545
Who and why?

78
00:09:22,655 --> 00:09:24,265
Come on, my Zulfiqar!

79
00:09:30,454 --> 00:09:31,624
Give us some space.

80
00:09:33,923 --> 00:09:35,013
Ya Allah!

81
00:09:38,182 --> 00:09:41,152
My Allah, take my life and give it to him.

82
00:09:44,534 --> 00:09:45,504
My Osman!

83
00:09:45,504 --> 00:09:47,684
My Osman, what did they do to you?

84
00:09:52,971 --> 00:09:54,371
Where did you find him?

85
00:09:54,371 --> 00:09:55,801
Who did this, son?

86
00:09:55,801 --> 00:09:57,331
We found him near Alacatepe.

87
00:09:57,331 --> 00:09:59,581
He was unconcious when we found him,
my Sheikh.

88
00:09:59,581 --> 00:10:03,081
Seems like he got hit by the arrow so
badly. We couldn't dare to touch it.

89
00:10:11,331 --> 00:10:13,461
What are we going to do?

90
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:20,926
Move aside!

91
00:10:46,371 --> 00:10:47,331
Osman!

92
00:10:48,635 --> 00:10:50,825
I am trying to prevent a conflict here.

93
00:10:50,825 --> 00:10:52,835
While you guys cast aspersions on me.

94
00:10:55,870 --> 00:10:56,990
Attack!

95
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:57,980
Kill them all!

96
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:59,030
Enough!

97
00:11:02,869 --> 00:11:04,039
Enough it is!

98
00:11:08,498 --> 00:11:10,448
What do you think you are doing?

99
00:11:10,798 --> 00:11:14,208
Brothers should not kill each other.

100
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:58,760
How dare you interrupt our fight?

101
00:11:58,825 --> 00:12:02,505
Don’t you know no Hatun is allowed
to stick her nose into important matters?

102
00:12:02,505 --> 00:12:03,575
Aygül Hatun!

103
00:12:03,774 --> 00:12:07,434
Don't mistake me with those Hatuns who
serve you at your mansion, Alişar Bey!

104
00:12:10,791 --> 00:12:11,901
I’m a Kayı.

105
00:12:14,510 --> 00:12:16,210
Sometimes, I’m a hatun...

106
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:18,000
... sometimes, a man!

107
00:12:21,523 --> 00:12:22,483
My daughter.

108
00:12:23,297 --> 00:12:24,777
You threw your hijab…

109
00:12:26,172 --> 00:12:27,612
…you want us to stop…

110
00:12:28,479 --> 00:12:29,309
...and...

111
00:12:30,129 --> 00:12:31,479
...im happy to do so.

112
00:12:31,593 --> 00:12:32,583
However...

113
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:35,770
...Alişar Bey says the opposite.

114
00:12:39,031 --> 00:12:41,411
You may get inside now.

115
00:12:46,722 --> 00:12:48,052
Brother Gūndūz.

116
00:12:48,637 --> 00:12:49,667
Bamsı Bey.

117
00:12:54,247 --> 00:12:56,487
Have you lost your patience?

118
00:12:58,503 --> 00:13:01,113
Why can’t you stand each other?

119
00:13:05,053 --> 00:13:07,833
What is this hostility and bloodshed
about?

120
00:13:09,652 --> 00:13:11,292
Aygül, my daughter…

121
00:13:12,896 --> 00:13:14,496
…nobody ever wanted…

122
00:13:14,496 --> 00:13:16,736
…what happened in the past.

123
00:13:21,163 --> 00:13:25,193
However, seditions your father once
planted...

124
00:13:27,425 --> 00:13:30,615
… has made nephews and uncles become
enemies...

125
00:13:30,615 --> 00:13:35,045
…as well as father-in laws and brides.

126
00:13:36,226 --> 00:13:38,056
My dear daughter, Aygül...

127
00:13:38,586 --> 00:13:42,126
…I have two arrow wounds on my shoulder…

128
00:13:44,645 --> 00:13:46,625
…and those very wounds are memories of…

129
00:13:47,293 --> 00:13:50,933
…Burçin, who I think of as my daughter.

130
00:13:54,656 --> 00:13:58,896
If that arrow had not hit you…

131
00:13:59,226 --> 00:14:01,336
…would you kill my Bahadır…

132
00:14:01,336 --> 00:14:03,426
…just like you killed my Batur?

133
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:13,670
Aygül.

134
00:14:14,551 --> 00:14:15,431
Burçin.

135
00:14:16,253 --> 00:14:17,223
You shall leave now.

136
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:18,393
Get inside.

137
00:14:55,633 --> 00:14:57,843
In the name of Allah...

138
00:14:59,715 --> 00:15:02,295
When I lay sick, he will take care of me
instead.

139
00:15:03,416 --> 00:15:04,966
May he be healed now.

140
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:14,960
Selcan Hatun!

141
00:15:15,966 --> 00:15:17,306
Is the fire ready?

142
00:15:17,488 --> 00:15:18,958
Yes, my Sheikh.

143
00:15:18,958 --> 00:15:20,258
How bad is his wound?

144
00:15:20,258 --> 00:15:21,278
It is egregious.

145
00:15:21,461 --> 00:15:24,621
If the arrow reached his lungs
we may have a hard time saving him.

146
00:15:24,621 --> 00:15:25,971
We will do our best.

147
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:29,180
Allah will have the final say.

148
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,630
May he be healed.

149
00:15:43,690 --> 00:15:45,440
He has massive bleeding, father.

150
00:15:51,387 --> 00:15:53,337
Resist, my lion.

151
00:15:53,337 --> 00:15:54,227
Resist.

152
00:15:56,942 --> 00:15:59,022
With the name of Allah.

153
00:16:06,895 --> 00:16:09,465
With the name of Allah.

154
00:16:41,465 --> 00:16:44,175
So that the hijab was thrown...

155
00:16:49,095 --> 00:16:52,819
...It’s not honorable to fight while
neglecting our customs.

156
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:56,499
Since the swords are down...

157
00:16:57,374 --> 00:16:58,974
I'll explain.

158
00:16:59,259 --> 00:17:03,279
You came to my door with questions and
curiosity.

159
00:17:05,971 --> 00:17:10,191
Because I neither corrupted Dündar Bey…

160
00:17:10,321 --> 00:17:15,291
…nor had a role in the murder of Batur.

161
00:17:22,370 --> 00:17:23,770
Now tell me…

162
00:17:25,674 --> 00:17:27,714
…what do you exactly want?

163
00:17:31,834 --> 00:17:35,194
From now on, you won’t interfere in our
domestic Tent affairs, Alişar.

164
00:17:36,981 --> 00:17:41,251
As a banner lord, every Tent located on
this Border are connected to me.

165
00:17:42,195 --> 00:17:43,675
What else can I do, Gündüz?

166
00:17:44,504 --> 00:17:45,704
Grow crops?

167
00:17:45,704 --> 00:17:47,044
Herd the cattle?

168
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:54,430
Now.

169
00:17:56,550 --> 00:17:57,310
Alişar.

170
00:17:59,243 --> 00:18:02,513
Other Tents at the Border may not say
something…

171
00:18:03,283 --> 00:18:04,493
…but...

172
00:18:05,073 --> 00:18:08,002
...a banner lord who interferes...

173
00:18:08,442 --> 00:18:10,302
...the Bey of Kayı and his people…

174
00:18:10,302 --> 00:18:12,202
...today...

175
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:15,732
…might try to interfere everyone tomorrow.

176
00:18:15,732 --> 00:18:17,692
They all know about this!

177
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,270
This is unacceptable, Alişar.

178
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,310
You will pay a high price.

179
00:18:29,013 --> 00:18:30,043
Gündüz Bey.

180
00:18:31,199 --> 00:18:32,199
Bamsı Bey.

181
00:18:35,255 --> 00:18:39,255
Once the order is broken
nobody will be able to fix it.

182
00:18:42,924 --> 00:18:47,904
I suggest we meet at Söğüt tomorrow.

183
00:18:51,093 --> 00:18:56,673
It’s your place and you can keep the area
safe wıth your horses.

184
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:06,268
Me and Dündar Bey will try to collaborate
with you.

185
00:19:08,692 --> 00:19:13,792
Instead of swords, we will use our words.

186
00:19:14,238 --> 00:19:17,588
It's a win-win situation for all.

187
00:19:36,327 --> 00:19:39,367
If you ever dare to play such games
wıth us again...

188
00:19:40,207 --> 00:19:42,797
…just for your information...

189
00:19:43,217 --> 00:19:47,497
...we wont lay our swords down again.

190
00:20:11,274 --> 00:20:13,724
Will he be okay, my Sheikh?

191
00:20:16,508 --> 00:20:19,718
Only Allah knows, Hatun.

192
00:20:21,082 --> 00:20:25,082
We should be positive so he'll be okay.

193
00:20:48,818 --> 00:20:52,258
in the name of Allah,
the compassionate, the merciful

194
00:21:01,383 --> 00:21:05,383
My Zulfiqar. Go and let the Kayı
Tent learn about his situation.

195
00:21:05,995 --> 00:21:08,235
We are in responsible
of Osman Bey’s life now.

196
00:21:08,235 --> 00:21:09,775
As you wish, my Sheikh

197
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:40,131
Salam Aleikum, my Sheikh.

198
00:21:40,176 --> 00:21:42,026
- Salam Aleikum.
- Aleikum Salam.

199
00:21:51,047 --> 00:21:54,027
Brother of Konur Alp,
Göktuğ Alp. My Sheikh.

200
00:21:54,027 --> 00:21:56,537
Thanks to Allah, he is a muslim now.

201
00:21:57,881 --> 00:21:59,531
Thanks to Allah.

202
00:22:05,307 --> 00:22:06,474
My Sheikh...

203
00:22:06,679 --> 00:22:08,084
...trails got us so far.

204
00:22:09,003 --> 00:22:10,219
Is Osman Bey here?

205
00:22:26,052 --> 00:22:27,108
Is he alright?

206
00:22:31,629 --> 00:22:34,359
What do you think you are doing, silly?

207
00:22:35,231 --> 00:22:37,303
You are ashaming me from
being your mother.

208
00:22:37,877 --> 00:22:40,048
Don't you still understand...

209
00:22:40,494 --> 00:22:42,787
...you are now the banner lord's wife!

210
00:22:43,572 --> 00:22:46,815
You are in his mansion, under his men's
protection!

211
00:22:47,628 --> 00:22:50,148
They all were going to die, stupid!

212
00:22:51,401 --> 00:22:53,587
Just because I'm Alişar's wife now...

213
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:55,767
...should I forget my past?

214
00:22:56,099 --> 00:22:59,008
Are Gündüz and Bamsı Bey stangers to us?

215
00:22:59,808 --> 00:23:02,008
This blood will drown us all.
Don't you see?

216
00:23:04,589 --> 00:23:06,827
If you are my mother...

217
00:23:07,381 --> 00:23:09,927
...think about our benefit and
sit down!

218
00:23:11,529 --> 00:23:15,387
But if it's like you said...

219
00:23:15,387 --> 00:23:18,349
...and I'm banner lord's wife,
then, know your place!

220
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:23,007
From now, it is my words that counts
in here!

221
00:23:27,146 --> 00:23:28,817
Aygül Hatun!

222
00:23:53,388 --> 00:23:57,514
I thought a Bey's daughter
would know her manners...

223
00:23:57,629 --> 00:24:00,748
...but you shame me in front of people...

224
00:24:00,847 --> 00:24:03,532
...how can you put off your hijab...

225
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:07,193
...when you were surrounded by men!

226
00:24:08,351 --> 00:24:11,488
What do you think you are doing with
this little brain of a woman!

227
00:24:16,619 --> 00:24:18,970
If you know how to raise that hand...

228
00:24:19,788 --> 00:24:21,888
...you should know how to use it, too.

229
00:24:23,762 --> 00:24:27,518
I wouldn't want your reputation to be
shaken in front of your warriors, husband.

230
00:24:28,988 --> 00:24:30,407
Come on.

231
00:24:55,281 --> 00:24:58,137
Don't wander around!
Don't make me beat you!

232
00:25:06,515 --> 00:25:09,014
You put off your hijab and lost my favor.

233
00:25:10,058 --> 00:25:11,660
Watch your wording.

234
00:25:12,178 --> 00:25:13,676
Don't lose my love, as well.

235
00:25:19,235 --> 00:25:22,274
If Noyans pledge alliance to me...

236
00:25:23,206 --> 00:25:26,156
...Geyhatu will see the might of
Balgay.

237
00:25:54,865 --> 00:25:56,892
You are smiling.

238
00:25:57,119 --> 00:25:59,456
Have you brought the news I desire?

239
00:25:59,592 --> 00:26:03,954
-We did, mighty Balgay.
-Don't forget. From now...

240
00:26:03,954 --> 00:26:06,838
...there is no brotherhood nor
companionship...

241
00:26:07,316 --> 00:26:09,542
...there is only Balgay.

242
00:26:10,145 --> 00:26:13,214
And a holy path...

243
00:26:13,515 --> 00:26:15,534
...to take with Balgay.

244
00:26:16,047 --> 00:26:18,555
We pledge you our lives and blood.

245
00:26:21,786 --> 00:26:23,336
Speak.

246
00:26:28,384 --> 00:26:31,278
Commander of Ankara, Kayseri and
Karaman...

247
00:26:32,055 --> 00:26:34,904
...they are all ready to stand with you
against Geyhatu.

248
00:26:35,826 --> 00:26:37,685
They wait for your word.

249
00:26:47,116 --> 00:26:49,154
If it wasn't for me...

250
00:26:49,613 --> 00:26:52,774
...you would be leashed by this Geyhatu...

251
00:26:53,714 --> 00:26:56,558
...who can't stay sober...

252
00:26:57,136 --> 00:27:00,180
...who sold his traditions to Buddha.

253
00:27:08,273 --> 00:27:10,214
Then...

254
00:27:10,704 --> 00:27:14,384
Move. Talha, Argun, Tuluy...

255
00:27:14,443 --> 00:27:17,860
...ride your horses without a break...

256
00:27:17,953 --> 00:27:20,516
...to Söğüt.

257
00:27:20,730 --> 00:27:23,261
May they race with the wind and
stop only for water.

258
00:27:24,212 --> 00:27:26,098
Tell them that...

259
00:27:26,448 --> 00:27:28,620
Geyhatu will come to Söğüt.

260
00:27:29,275 --> 00:27:30,933
Tell them to join me...

261
00:27:31,757 --> 00:27:34,855
...to cut off his head.

262
00:27:34,953 --> 00:27:37,020
That head of his which smiles like...

263
00:27:37,704 --> 00:27:39,893
...sinister face of Buddha.

264
00:27:39,893 --> 00:27:41,385
As you order, Commander Balgay.

265
00:27:50,935 --> 00:27:53,675
Geyhatu sent a vanguard.

266
00:27:54,140 --> 00:27:56,159
They are coming from the Karaayaz Forest.

267
00:27:56,334 --> 00:27:58,054
Let's go there and see...

268
00:27:58,516 --> 00:28:00,676
...what's the problem of this drunkard.

269
00:28:31,245 --> 00:28:32,724
Dear Allah...

270
00:28:33,664 --> 00:28:36,853
Give us the strength to bear this pain...

271
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,301
Don't give me the pain of losing a
child.

272
00:28:47,312 --> 00:28:49,574
Don't give me the pain of
losing Osman.

273
00:28:58,745 --> 00:29:00,921
My lion is burning...

274
00:29:02,017 --> 00:29:03,617
I'll bring water.

275
00:29:03,837 --> 00:29:05,665
Don't leave him alone.

276
00:29:07,884 --> 00:29:09,077
Bala.

277
00:29:13,603 --> 00:29:14,494
Bala.

278
00:29:16,114 --> 00:29:17,945
Keep your head up!

279
00:29:18,847 --> 00:29:21,341
It's not the time to be sad.

280
00:29:21,773 --> 00:29:23,586
It's time to seek Allah's help.

281
00:29:26,674 --> 00:29:28,837
Osman both hears and feels us.

282
00:29:30,762 --> 00:29:33,041
If you want him to wake up...

283
00:29:33,839 --> 00:29:35,453
...take that tear away.

284
00:29:36,898 --> 00:29:39,054
Keep your head up and wait.

285
00:30:04,109 --> 00:30:05,243
Osman.

286
00:30:07,090 --> 00:30:09,075
Do you really hear me?

287
00:30:11,525 --> 00:30:15,128
Do you feel how my heart hurts?

288
00:30:25,947 --> 00:30:27,933
I beg you, wake up.

289
00:30:31,611 --> 00:30:35,570
You are my hope, luck, and future.

290
00:30:39,364 --> 00:30:41,960
What can I do without you?

291
00:30:44,957 --> 00:30:46,684
I will fall apart.

292
00:30:52,971 --> 00:30:54,989
Don't break me further.

293
00:30:57,337 --> 00:30:59,041
Wake up, I beg you.

294
00:31:18,385 --> 00:31:20,009
My Allah...

295
00:31:21,188 --> 00:31:23,372
...help him.

296
00:32:16,591 --> 00:32:18,341
What is wrong, Zülfikar Dervish?

297
00:32:20,122 --> 00:32:21,555
Welcome.

298
00:32:22,343 --> 00:32:24,552
But I'm afraid it's not a
pleasant visit.

299
00:32:25,517 --> 00:32:26,938
Gündüz Bey...

300
00:32:27,464 --> 00:32:29,339
...Sheikh Edebali sent me.

301
00:32:32,472 --> 00:32:34,037
About Osman Bey.

302
00:32:35,259 --> 00:32:36,675
Osman?

303
00:32:37,627 --> 00:32:40,179
Where is my brother, dervish?
Tell us.

304
00:32:41,418 --> 00:32:43,288
Dervishes had found him in
the forest.

305
00:32:45,505 --> 00:32:47,863
He was severely wounded when
they brought him.

306
00:32:48,541 --> 00:32:51,750
Sheikh stepped in quickly. And he sent
word to you.

307
00:32:52,281 --> 00:32:55,008
''He is under our protection.
Don't you worry.'' he said.

308
00:32:56,235 --> 00:32:59,572
What are we waiting for, then?

309
00:33:00,090 --> 00:33:03,278
We should go to Osman, right away!

310
00:33:04,228 --> 00:33:05,460
Hold on, Bamsı Bey.

311
00:33:06,597 --> 00:33:07,586
Hold on.

312
00:33:11,872 --> 00:33:14,972
Inform Kongur Alp. Go
to Osman with the dervish.

313
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:16,523
Yes, my Bey.

314
00:33:18,583 --> 00:33:21,325
Bamsı Bey, we will go to
Söğüt...

315
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:24,751
...to face Alişar.

316
00:33:27,834 --> 00:33:29,533
Abdurrahman ghazi...

317
00:33:29,752 --> 00:33:33,899
...the tent is under your responsibility.
-Yes, Gündüz Bey.

318
00:33:35,586 --> 00:33:38,097
Dervish, don't leave Osman alone.

319
00:33:39,249 --> 00:33:41,170
If you need anything...

320
00:33:42,273 --> 00:33:43,849
...inform us.

321
00:33:45,180 --> 00:33:47,177
May Allah help Osman...

322
00:33:47,956 --> 00:33:49,620
...and reunite us, inshallah.

323
00:33:50,075 --> 00:33:51,530
-Inshallah, Gündüz Bey.
-Amin.

324
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:57,106
The memory of Aybars...

325
00:33:57,599 --> 00:33:59,817
...is still a wound in my heart.

326
00:34:01,815 --> 00:34:03,225
Gündüz...

327
00:34:03,561 --> 00:34:05,896
...I must see Osman.

328
00:34:06,254 --> 00:34:07,831
I have to, Gündüz. I have to!

329
00:34:08,353 --> 00:34:10,665
Bamsı Bey, if Osman was here...

330
00:34:11,310 --> 00:34:13,661
...he would want you to be with me.

331
00:34:15,032 --> 00:34:18,650
Do you think that there is no other
traitors than Şahin and Demirci Bey?

332
00:34:21,071 --> 00:34:22,631
We are surrounded.

333
00:34:24,249 --> 00:34:26,967
Time isn't our friend.

334
00:34:36,590 --> 00:34:39,220
Dervish, dervish...

335
00:34:39,542 --> 00:34:40,713
Bamsı Bey.

336
00:34:40,924 --> 00:34:44,544
Now when you see that Osman
opens his eyes...

337
00:34:44,835 --> 00:34:49,460
...when Bamsı Bey completes his
mission...

338
00:34:49,775 --> 00:34:52,549
...he will come there. Say that, will you?

339
00:34:52,919 --> 00:34:54,680
-Of course.
-Thank you.

340
00:34:55,655 --> 00:34:57,296
-Thank you.

341
00:35:04,947 --> 00:35:07,144
These are our best soldiers, my Bey.

342
00:35:07,902 --> 00:35:10,439
With a bow, they can shoot a flying bird..

343
00:35:11,301 --> 00:35:14,016
...with a sword, they can slain a dragon.

344
00:35:20,871 --> 00:35:22,222
Alişar Bey.

345
00:35:23,188 --> 00:35:25,003
We got into this together...

346
00:35:25,142 --> 00:35:28,301
We have done everything together...

347
00:35:28,459 --> 00:35:32,256
How can you say that you will
kill me, too?

348
00:35:37,389 --> 00:35:41,295
Revenge is a dish best served cold...

349
00:35:41,365 --> 00:35:42,608
...Dündar Bey.

350
00:35:43,560 --> 00:35:45,172
Don't catch fire.

351
00:35:46,021 --> 00:35:47,604
Control your anger.

352
00:35:49,453 --> 00:35:52,897
What kind of revenge is that?
What kind of alliance is that?

353
00:35:54,132 --> 00:35:56,571
You speak of killing us,
in front of our enemies.

354
00:35:56,919 --> 00:35:59,032
Don't hurry, Bahadır.

355
00:36:00,176 --> 00:36:02,368
We skinned it...

356
00:36:03,079 --> 00:36:04,567
...now we are on it's tail.

357
00:36:04,833 --> 00:36:08,137
What is left is putting some salt
and waiting.

358
00:36:10,639 --> 00:36:14,536
Killing Beys who came to my door
would bring trouble.

359
00:36:19,624 --> 00:36:23,421
We will ambush Bamsı and Gündüz
on their way to Söğüt.

360
00:36:26,028 --> 00:36:28,973
With my most elite troops.

361
00:36:31,057 --> 00:36:33,455
They have no hope now.

362
00:36:35,573 --> 00:36:38,570
While we are waiting for them...

363
00:36:39,332 --> 00:36:41,933
...their dead bodies will come.

364
00:37:09,591 --> 00:37:18,590
Aid! Sahibel Meydan!

365
00:37:21,106 --> 00:37:28,652
May I call you with mountains and rocks...

366
00:37:31,435 --> 00:37:38,454
May I call you with birds at dawn...

367
00:37:39,208 --> 00:37:44,413
May I call you, my protector.

368
00:37:45,963 --> 00:37:50,097
With Ayyub who has the most troubles...

369
00:37:52,192 --> 00:37:58,176
...and Yakub with his tears on his eyes...

370
00:38:02,935 --> 00:38:08,264
O' Muhammed! With love...

371
00:38:09,194 --> 00:38:13,437
...may I call you, my protector.

372
00:38:29,478 --> 00:38:34,087
With beautiful nightingales...

373
00:38:34,422 --> 00:38:40,784
With followers who love Allah...

374
00:38:46,661 --> 00:38:52,801
May I call you, my protector.

375
00:39:00,823 --> 00:39:06,192
Aid! Tabibel-Kulub.

376
00:39:46,114 --> 00:39:47,596
Dear Allah...

377
00:39:48,969 --> 00:39:51,415
...I seek your protection...

378
00:39:52,039 --> 00:39:54,630
...from disrespecting your words.

379
00:40:12,199 --> 00:40:13,564
My Allah...

380
00:40:15,921 --> 00:40:17,549
...you...

381
00:40:20,153 --> 00:40:22,467
...take me and my lineage...

382
00:40:24,467 --> 00:40:26,337
...to ones who sacrifice...

383
00:40:27,776 --> 00:40:30,224
...for your words.

384
00:41:25,196 --> 00:41:28,175
Help, Sahibel Meydan!

385
00:41:30,836 --> 00:41:37,561
May I call you with mountains and rocks...

386
00:41:40,898 --> 00:41:47,443
May I call you with birds at dawn...

387
00:41:48,266 --> 00:41:53,208
May I call you, my protector.

388
00:41:55,706 --> 00:41:58,643
With Ayyub who has the most troubles...

389
00:42:01,506 --> 00:42:07,218
...and Yakub with his tears on his eyes...

390
00:42:08,508 --> 00:42:13,549
O' Muhammed! With love...

391
00:42:14,292 --> 00:42:17,293
...may I call you, my protector.

392
00:42:18,035 --> 00:42:22,883
...may I call you, my protector.

393
00:42:25,842 --> 00:42:30,444
With Hamd ü şükrullah...

394
00:42:38,883 --> 00:42:42,865
With beautiful nightingales...

395
00:42:49,259 --> 00:42:53,604
With followers who love Allah...

396
00:43:01,020 --> 00:43:06,661
May I call you, my protector.

397
00:43:10,033 --> 00:43:14,670
Aid! Tabibel-Kulub.

398
00:44:06,493 --> 00:44:21,453
Allah is the greatest.

399
00:44:27,924 --> 00:44:37,164
I bear witness that there is no lord
except for Allah.

400
00:44:37,164 --> 00:44:47,794
Oh my Lord.

401
00:45:13,371 --> 00:45:15,741
Oh my Lord.

402
00:45:22,612 --> 00:45:25,712
May it be good.

403
00:45:27,649 --> 00:45:30,759
May it be good.

404
00:46:07,837 --> 00:46:11,557
In the name of Allah,
the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.

405
00:46:12,664 --> 00:46:18,864
Indeed, We have given you, [O Muhammad], a clear conquest
[Quran Al-Fath 48:1]

406
00:46:21,950 --> 00:46:26,020
Allaah Almighty has spoken the truth

407
00:47:31,215 --> 00:47:33,825
What is it, son?

408
00:47:34,907 --> 00:47:37,437
What is bothering you?

409
00:47:44,479 --> 00:47:49,649
I tried to stay awake but...

410
00:47:50,128 --> 00:47:56,198
I fell asleep due to tiredness.

411
00:48:03,016 --> 00:48:05,316
When I was sleeping...

412
00:48:06,808 --> 00:48:11,108
I saw such a dream that...

413
00:48:15,274 --> 00:48:17,844
Tell me, son.

414
00:48:29,294 --> 00:48:31,604
In my dream...

415
00:48:36,379 --> 00:48:43,049
A moon rose from your chest
and dive in my mine.

416
00:48:45,988 --> 00:48:50,088
My chest shaked, expanded...

417
00:48:51,418 --> 00:48:54,132
...and enlightened.

418
00:48:58,434 --> 00:49:00,744
Then...

419
00:49:01,960 --> 00:49:08,050
Something came out of my chest and
greatened so much that...

420
00:49:10,022 --> 00:49:14,612
That almighty tree's branches...

421
00:49:15,813 --> 00:49:17,693
...exceeded this universe...

422
00:49:20,651 --> 00:49:23,831
...and arrived at beyond the seas.

423
00:49:26,870 --> 00:49:30,690
It covered many realms...

424
00:49:33,466 --> 00:49:37,286
...in vast lands.

425
00:49:43,419 --> 00:49:46,406
I saw weapons there.

426
00:49:46,406 --> 00:49:49,596
Weapons that are bloody.

427
00:49:50,923 --> 00:49:53,243
I saw minarets.

428
00:49:55,001 --> 00:50:00,721
On top of minarets, I saw crescents.

429
00:50:04,950 --> 00:50:07,240
May it be good.

430
00:50:09,129 --> 00:50:12,339
May it be good, my Sheik.

431
00:50:15,329 --> 00:50:17,859
What is it?

432
00:50:21,682 --> 00:50:24,542
Osman Bey...

433
00:50:25,174 --> 00:50:30,234
Ertuğrul Ghazi's pride,
Dark Osman Bey.

434
00:50:32,512 --> 00:50:35,072
Valiant Osman.

435
00:50:35,657 --> 00:50:43,147
In your dream, you came to me, so
our Lord wants us together.

436
00:50:46,655 --> 00:50:53,425
You said a moon rose from my chest
and dive in yours.

437
00:50:55,366 --> 00:50:58,366
It is time.

438
00:50:59,779 --> 00:51:03,409
From now on, I give permission.

439
00:51:05,512 --> 00:51:09,882
Bala Hatun is your halal (permissible).

440
00:51:12,966 --> 00:51:17,916
Because this is a divine sign.

441
00:51:23,053 --> 00:51:31,633
Allah granted your generation Khanship,
and Sultanate.

442
00:51:37,214 --> 00:51:46,414
Many places will be Islam city with your
and your generation's efforts.

443
00:53:42,991 --> 00:53:46,351
Geyhatu's corrupts!

444
00:53:46,642 --> 00:53:49,532
Kill them all!

445
00:54:23,483 --> 00:54:26,043
Balgay! You traitor!

446
00:54:28,149 --> 00:54:31,399
Damn you!

447
00:55:23,658 --> 00:55:26,008
What is Geyhatu saying?

448
00:55:27,390 --> 00:55:30,289
They are coming here.

449
00:55:30,289 --> 00:55:33,759
They departed from Konya.

450
00:55:33,786 --> 00:55:39,046
He ordered his dog Alişar to
hang Osman in Söğüt bazaar...

451
00:55:39,182 --> 00:55:44,892
...and wipe Kayı Alps off.

452
00:55:47,066 --> 00:55:51,906
We are going to preapre a great
welcoming ceremony to Geyhatu.

453
00:55:58,519 --> 00:56:04,359
Thunder will shake Konya while...

454
00:56:05,443 --> 00:56:11,373
Lightnings cover everywhere.

455
00:56:18,347 --> 00:56:23,107
Come to your death, Geyhatu.

456
00:56:23,744 --> 00:56:26,444
Come to your death.

457
00:57:04,869 --> 00:57:09,929
I said it earlier, my daughter.
Everything has its time.

458
00:57:11,844 --> 00:57:16,044
Your time to marry Osman Bey
has arrived.

459
00:57:24,868 --> 00:57:29,198
Osman Bey is like a peak of a mountain.

460
00:57:29,550 --> 00:57:36,230
Stand everything about him.

461
00:57:37,425 --> 00:57:41,865
His way is difficult, his enemies are
tough.

462
00:57:44,347 --> 00:57:48,667
Don't make a mistake while keeping
company.

463
00:58:00,173 --> 00:58:02,793
Thank Lord.

464
00:58:09,387 --> 00:58:15,232
You wanted my Bala for Osman earlier...

465
00:58:15,232 --> 00:58:19,912
...but we didn't give her because it
was not the right time.

466
00:58:22,481 --> 00:58:27,321
Now, the day has come.

467
00:58:30,700 --> 00:58:34,650
Inform your tribe's almighty ones at once.

468
00:58:34,709 --> 00:58:38,789
Your tribe's almighties shall come too.

469
00:58:39,902 --> 00:58:44,212
There will be a marriage ceremony
as soon as possible.

470
00:58:47,619 --> 00:58:54,429
The sign shows us that, when we establish
this blessed event here...

471
00:58:54,442 --> 00:58:58,182
there will be
other things to establish, too.

472
00:59:08,124 --> 00:59:12,254
However you deem appropriate, my Sheik.

473
00:59:17,772 --> 00:59:21,812
- Thank Lord.
- Thank Lord.

474
00:59:41,163 --> 00:59:44,113
You talk about Söğüt Han, Alişar Bey.

475
00:59:44,334 --> 00:59:49,064
What are you thinking?
Why do you have the talk there?

476
00:59:50,070 --> 00:59:57,465
We wıll wait in front of Kayı Alps in
Söğütlü.

477
00:59:57,465 --> 01:00:03,235
When they bring us Gündüz and Bamsı's
bodies...

478
01:00:03,273 --> 01:00:07,823
No one will doubt that we did this.

479
01:00:10,994 --> 01:00:15,944
What happened, Dündar Bey?
You seem unhappy.

480
01:00:17,271 --> 01:00:23,021
No, I think about Osman, Alişar Bey.

481
01:00:23,330 --> 01:00:30,320
What if Geyhatu forgives him?
What if he creates trouble again?

482
01:00:30,508 --> 01:00:36,838
He is angry as hell, don't you know Osman?

483
01:00:36,992 --> 01:00:43,862
Even if Genghiz Khan resurrect, no one
can take Osman from my hands.

484
01:00:45,006 --> 01:00:48,786
He is dead now.

485
01:00:50,471 --> 01:00:52,991
What is the situation, brother Boran?

486
01:00:53,421 --> 01:00:58,291
They killed Kılıç Alp where Zöhre Hatun
was waiting, my Bey.

487
01:00:58,985 --> 01:01:03,628
Not only that...
They also shot Bamsı Bey.

488
01:01:03,628 --> 01:01:06,221
What are you talking about, Boran?

489
01:01:06,221 --> 01:01:09,841
- Who shot Bamsı Bey?
- Burçin Hatun, my Bey.

490
01:01:10,110 --> 01:01:12,060
What?

491
01:01:16,072 --> 01:01:18,322
Burçin...

492
01:01:21,717 --> 01:01:26,007
So, they poisoned Burçin too.

493
01:01:26,328 --> 01:01:30,878
I am afraid that, if we don't stop them...

494
01:01:31,029 --> 01:01:34,349
they will poison everyone.

495
01:01:36,480 --> 01:01:43,160
- What did my brother do?
- He went to Alişar's mansion to take revenge.

496
01:01:43,225 --> 01:01:48,785
However, they wanted to come to Söğüt.
They want an agreement.

497
01:01:48,818 --> 01:01:53,428
Eh, black snake!
He surely knows we can't agree.

498
01:01:54,993 --> 01:01:58,776
He is afriad to kill Beys in front of
his mansion.

499
01:01:58,776 --> 01:02:02,426
That's why he used the.

500
01:02:06,440 --> 01:02:13,040
I think they will attack, but we will
act faster than him.

501
01:02:13,443 --> 01:02:17,370
My Bey, Dündar Bey will come too.

502
01:02:17,370 --> 01:02:23,550
It's over now, brother.
Blood must shed!

503
01:02:26,091 --> 01:02:31,781
Both my uncle's and Bahadır's death
are near.

504
01:02:33,906 --> 01:02:38,296
Göktuğ.
Take Çetin with you.

505
01:02:40,713 --> 01:02:48,703
Now, you'll be Kongar so that
you can approach to Balgay.

506
01:02:49,047 --> 01:02:56,757
You will spy on them and tell
me where they settle.

507
01:02:58,271 --> 01:03:03,031
The most important card will be
Balgay for Geyhatu.

508
01:03:03,154 --> 01:03:05,804
Yes, Osman Bey.

509
01:03:08,024 --> 01:03:11,854
Boran, listen to me carefully now.

510
01:03:12,011 --> 01:03:16,271
Tell what I tell you to my brother.

511
01:03:17,955 --> 01:03:25,485
Alişar will do his best to push us.

512
01:03:26,161 --> 01:03:28,851
He will, Bamsı Bey.

513
01:03:30,558 --> 01:03:34,108
What if we can't agree, son?

514
01:03:35,510 --> 01:03:40,430
Then, the most honourable place
would be waiting for us.

515
01:03:40,745 --> 01:03:47,535
We die with honor and be martyr instead
of obeying the cruel, in sha Allah.

516
01:03:48,257 --> 01:03:53,726
Oh, my Gündüz, how beautiful you speak!

517
01:03:53,726 --> 01:03:59,109
If there is shahada in the end,
we can't wait.

518
01:03:59,109 --> 01:04:06,219
Let's go, son.
Let's see, whatever happens, happens.

519
01:04:17,991 --> 01:04:21,871
Hey, Mashallah (praise be)
My Valiants!

520
01:04:21,871 --> 01:04:25,431
Mashallah my lions!
Let's go my valiants!

521
01:04:26,050 --> 01:04:29,700
Let's go, valiants!

522
01:05:00,107 --> 01:05:02,727
We found them.

523
01:05:05,451 --> 01:05:08,521
They even setup a base.

524
01:05:11,193 --> 01:05:15,063
Çetin, inform Osman Bey.

525
01:05:15,063 --> 01:05:17,773
Quite.

526
01:05:30,033 --> 01:05:33,673
Come, Geyhatu.

527
01:05:34,154 --> 01:05:41,264
Come and see what Erlik Khan does to you!

528
01:06:02,741 --> 01:06:03,831
Balgay!

529
01:06:04,631 --> 01:06:05,781
Kongar is coming.

530
01:06:10,027 --> 01:06:12,647
Do you think he has Genghis Khan's laws?

531
01:06:32,455 --> 01:06:34,635
Where are the Genghis Khan's laws?

532
01:06:34,635 --> 01:06:36,655
That dog Osman lied again.

533
01:06:37,205 --> 01:06:39,935
Boran tried to kill the Nökers
and run away.

534
01:06:40,223 --> 01:06:41,923
I cut his throat.

535
01:06:43,932 --> 01:06:45,332
Where is Osman?

536
01:06:45,332 --> 01:06:48,082
He ran away with an arrow on his back.

537
01:06:50,945 --> 01:06:53,095
As if he has 9 lives.

538
01:06:54,154 --> 01:06:56,734
We'll meet again, eventually.

539
01:07:09,247 --> 01:07:11,717
Focus on ending Bamsı with an arrow.

540
01:07:12,217 --> 01:07:16,527
Then use your swords.
Don't let his age fool you.

541
01:07:16,762 --> 01:07:20,762
He'll turn into a dragon
the moment he gets your smell.

542
01:07:46,954 --> 01:07:50,014
Why aren't they here already?
Did something go wrong?

543
01:07:51,517 --> 01:07:52,687
Ambush!

544
01:08:39,206 --> 01:08:40,336
Soldiers!

545
01:08:47,814 --> 01:08:49,324
Soldiers!

546
01:09:25,208 --> 01:09:26,758
Osman Bey...

547
01:09:27,568 --> 01:09:29,778
I'll tell you everything
if you spare my life.

548
01:09:30,947 --> 01:09:34,157
I beg you, don't.
I know a lot.

549
01:09:52,327 --> 01:09:55,967
Another trouble begins before one ends.

550
01:09:56,280 --> 01:09:58,480
But this is the last one.

551
01:10:01,179 --> 01:10:03,949
Your age has started.

552
01:10:04,526 --> 01:10:07,546
May your Beyhood be blessed.

553
01:10:10,300 --> 01:10:13,910
Thank you, Alişar Bey.
Thank you.

554
01:10:14,243 --> 01:10:21,853
I wish they left me another choice so
they wouldn't have lost their lives.

555
01:10:22,451 --> 01:10:29,821
I wish they didn't ruin their lives by
following Osman and his empty dreams.

556
01:10:29,882 --> 01:10:35,282
They wanted this.
They did everything to die.

557
01:10:56,694 --> 01:10:59,664
Bamsı Bey, welcome!
Welcome!

558
01:10:59,664 --> 01:11:03,664
Gündüz!
Bamsı Bey!

559
01:11:08,262 --> 01:11:10,262
How can this be, Alişar Bey?

560
01:11:12,796 --> 01:11:15,476
Something fish is going on.

561
01:11:16,085 --> 01:11:19,235
It was impossible for them
to get out of that ambush alive.

562
01:11:21,332 --> 01:11:24,362
I told you to be careful countless times.

563
01:11:25,065 --> 01:11:27,035
What will we do now, Alişar Bey?

564
01:11:49,081 --> 01:11:53,461
My Boran! Is my Osman okay?
I hope nothing is wrong.

565
01:11:53,625 --> 01:11:56,715
He's okay, my Bey.
He knows that we're going to söğüt.

566
01:11:56,861 --> 01:12:00,861
But my Bey said that there were traps
everywhere. Don't take the jungle route.

567
01:12:01,241 --> 01:12:03,481
Go from the Alacatepe foothill.

568
01:13:37,476 --> 01:13:45,356
My father was a famous Noyan
besides almighty Genghis Khan.

569
01:13:47,216 --> 01:13:52,796
When Genghis Khan went to save
his wife Börti from Merkits...

570
01:13:53,536 --> 01:13:55,396
... my father was with him.

571
01:13:56,929 --> 01:14:02,159
While they were going to save
that almighty, powerful woman...

572
01:14:03,500 --> 01:14:06,750
... do you know what
Genghis Khan said to my father?

573
01:14:08,362 --> 01:14:14,082
Don't come if you're afraid.
If you'll come, don't be afraid.

574
01:14:19,343 --> 01:14:23,923
Your path is my path. I won't turn back.

575
01:14:25,027 --> 01:14:29,197
You raised me like Cuci,
son of the raped Börte Hatun.

576
01:14:30,534 --> 01:14:35,944
My destiny with Cuci is the same.
We were both naive children.

577
01:14:37,820 --> 01:14:42,780
But you protected me.

578
01:14:44,954 --> 01:14:47,164
You were a father to me.

579
01:14:50,789 --> 01:14:55,719
I named you while I was washing your
face with warm water in River Selengi.

580
01:15:03,516 --> 01:15:08,336
You were a scared, cold, naked child.

581
01:15:12,636 --> 01:15:14,386
You were nothing.

582
01:15:16,246 --> 01:15:19,176
I created you from nothing.

583
01:15:28,969 --> 01:15:31,059
What is that is bothering you, Balgay?

584
01:15:32,757 --> 01:15:34,077
Osman?

585
01:15:41,854 --> 01:15:48,584
What if he takes you from me
like Genghis Khan's laws?

586
01:15:51,339 --> 01:15:53,919
I swore upon this.

587
01:15:55,714 --> 01:15:59,474
I won't die without killing him.

588
01:16:01,814 --> 01:16:03,244
I know.

589
01:16:06,388 --> 01:16:11,038
Since you know it,
then what is that's bothering you?

590
01:16:12,913 --> 01:16:14,203
Father...

591
01:16:17,666 --> 01:16:22,676
You're my father, my mother,
and my ancestor.

592
01:16:23,657 --> 01:16:26,807
The rest is nothing for me
like the Gobi desert.

593
01:16:28,343 --> 01:16:34,813
I'm a Mongol. I'll die fighting on
a horse like a real Mongol.

594
01:16:36,921 --> 01:16:42,121
Nothing can change my love
and loyalty for you.

595
01:17:12,993 --> 01:17:18,323
What is it, Alişar Bey?
You look surprised.

596
01:17:18,880 --> 01:17:24,680
There's nothing to be surprised about.
We called you and you came.

597
01:17:24,826 --> 01:17:28,826
Now we'll talk nicely.

598
01:17:28,826 --> 01:17:34,576
Oh, nope. Dündar Bey looks like
he saw a monster.

599
01:17:37,763 --> 01:17:39,583
May it be blessed.

600
01:17:43,816 --> 01:17:49,346
You caused a lot of trouble.
Now, tell us what you want!

601
01:17:49,568 --> 01:17:54,208
In our Tent, we want those
who are after a bloody war.

602
01:17:56,732 --> 01:18:01,282
Give us my uncle Dündar and Bahadır.

603
01:18:03,933 --> 01:18:06,533
And don't be involved in
our Tent's internal affairs.

604
01:18:12,627 --> 01:18:16,627
If you want them,
you must get through me.

605
01:18:23,488 --> 01:18:25,708
About your internal affairs...

606
01:18:26,517 --> 01:18:32,377
Don't you know that all the Tents
in these lands are connected to me?

607
01:18:32,377 --> 01:18:37,027
We're connected to our traditiıons
, not you, Alişar Bey.

608
01:18:39,040 --> 01:18:46,030
We've come to these lands for holy war,
not for brute force.

609
01:18:47,420 --> 01:18:51,880
You're talking about traditions.
But you don't know that...

610
01:18:51,880 --> 01:18:57,240
... a Tent is connected to a Bey and a
Bey is connected to a Banner Lord, Gündüz.

611
01:18:57,661 --> 01:19:03,891
Salurs, Dodurgas, AlkaEvlis
also live in these lands.

612
01:19:05,042 --> 01:19:07,512
They don't cause trouble.

613
01:19:09,053 --> 01:19:12,783
Why is it you who always causes trouble?

614
01:19:14,301 --> 01:19:21,901
Remember this. This provision of yours
will be the rope that hangs you.

615
01:19:22,016 --> 01:19:25,546
Are you threatening me?

616
01:19:26,374 --> 01:19:30,374
Who do you think you are?
Pull yourselves together!

617
01:19:45,205 --> 01:19:46,575
Alps!

618
01:20:02,281 --> 01:20:06,961
Hear my words, Alişar.

619
01:20:07,214 --> 01:20:11,874
Beys are not happy with you being
involved in Kayı's young men...

620
01:20:11,874 --> 01:20:23,154
... assigning Beys, and trying to remove
a Bey from the throne with a bloody war.

621
01:20:24,864 --> 01:20:30,164
They are scared as
to when it will be their turn.

622
01:20:49,210 --> 01:20:55,510
Since the Turks are
so anxious and displeased...

623
01:20:56,271 --> 01:20:58,871
... then as the Bey of these lands...

624
01:20:59,911 --> 01:21:02,611
... I'll assign a Bey from the Çavdars!

625
01:21:03,786 --> 01:21:07,786
Alişar Bey...

626
01:21:07,986 --> 01:21:11,356
These lands are our sword-given rights.

627
01:21:12,067 --> 01:21:15,087
What does it mean to make
a Mongol the land's Bey?

628
01:21:15,087 --> 01:21:19,087
These lands belong to Geyhatu!

629
01:21:19,763 --> 01:21:22,233
He takes the seal from
whoever he wants to.

630
01:21:22,233 --> 01:21:24,893
And gives the throne
to whoever he wants to.

631
01:21:28,775 --> 01:21:33,615
Do you think the Beys
in these lands will obey these orders?

632
01:21:34,441 --> 01:21:37,581
This is the border, Alişar Bey!

633
01:21:38,210 --> 01:21:42,210
Do you recognize?
It's not like the place you've come from.

634
01:21:42,611 --> 01:21:46,611
Which of the Oghuz Tents will obey them?

635
01:21:48,770 --> 01:21:54,330
They either bow
or get their heads cut off.

636
01:21:56,197 --> 01:21:58,687
I said everything necessary.

637
01:21:59,691 --> 01:22:08,371
You'll tell these to Geyhatu
when he personally stands in front of you.

638
01:22:11,519 --> 01:22:14,539
You're trusting Geyhatu to protect you.

639
01:22:17,173 --> 01:22:19,763
We're trusting Allah.

640
01:22:26,417 --> 01:22:31,297
Come on, then.
Do everything you can.

641
01:23:18,479 --> 01:23:19,749
Let's go!

642
01:23:21,373 --> 01:23:22,583
Let's go!

643
01:23:23,373 --> 01:23:26,393
By Allah! Let's go!

644
01:23:57,600 --> 01:24:01,230
You found that dog's nest
since you came alone, Çetin.

645
01:24:01,357 --> 01:24:06,257
We did thankfully, my Bey. Göktuğ is
with Balgay. He's waiting for us.

646
01:24:06,257 --> 01:24:11,207
- Praise be! My lion!
- Thank you, my Bey!

647
01:24:11,327 --> 01:24:16,517
But Balgay is crafty. He might realize
Göktuğ is working with us.

648
01:24:17,078 --> 01:24:22,538
We shouldn't let a jackal strangle
our lion. Let's get going. Let's go!

649
01:24:28,620 --> 01:24:36,350
It's too late. Geyhatu
will decide Kayı's fate.

650
01:24:37,303 --> 01:24:44,913
It will be a little bloody. You'll
eventually get your throne, Dündar Bey.

651
01:24:45,489 --> 01:24:49,489
You're right, Alişar Bey.
You're right.

652
01:24:52,055 --> 01:24:55,895
- I'm worried about Melik.
- Alişar Bey...

653
01:24:57,475 --> 01:24:59,895
... they either didn't fall into
the trap...

654
01:25:00,085 --> 01:25:05,735
... or Melik, that master
hunter of yours, was hunted.

655
01:25:07,475 --> 01:25:10,115
What if they made him talk like Zorba?

656
01:25:10,615 --> 01:25:12,825
He knows a lot about our alliance.

657
01:25:15,079 --> 01:25:20,159
Then I'll show them my wrath!

658
01:25:21,490 --> 01:25:27,220
We're going into the woods!
We'll trace Melik!

659
01:25:58,751 --> 01:26:02,051
Alps! Come on. Go this way.

660
01:26:15,555 --> 01:26:17,545
My Bey! Someone is coming!

661
01:26:51,852 --> 01:26:56,982
Keep your eyes open. Don't forget
what'll happen if they find us.

662
01:26:57,897 --> 01:26:59,057
Let's go.

663
01:27:21,397 --> 01:27:23,467
What's the situation, Göktuğ?

664
01:27:23,467 --> 01:27:26,397
Balgay destroyed a unit of Geyhatu.

665
01:27:26,720 --> 01:27:30,480
He's preparing to gather other units
that'll fight against him.

666
01:27:32,257 --> 01:27:36,257
Geyhatu is preparing to kill Balgay
when he comes to Söğüt.

667
01:27:36,429 --> 01:27:39,499
My Bey! Exactly as you wanted!

668
01:27:42,268 --> 01:27:45,558
It's time to let dogs fight
each other, brothers.

669
01:27:50,214 --> 01:27:52,224
Listen to me carefully.

670
01:27:59,523 --> 01:28:02,033
The unit coming with Geyhatu
is very crowded.

671
01:28:02,686 --> 01:28:05,816
It'll take your loyal commanders
days to come.

672
01:28:06,138 --> 01:28:13,048
When Geyhatu comes,
I'll throw Kayıs at him first.

673
01:28:15,748 --> 01:28:22,748
Kayıs are strong. While Geyhatu is busy
with causing Osman's extinction...

674
01:28:22,923 --> 01:28:26,923
... my commanders will be here.
Then we'll start moving.

675
01:28:27,185 --> 01:28:28,565
What about Osman?

676
01:28:29,018 --> 01:28:32,138
You can't fight if you feel
the enemy on your back.

677
01:28:32,138 --> 01:28:34,228
When Osman comes...

678
01:28:36,547 --> 01:28:38,357
Ambush!

679
01:28:41,815 --> 01:28:43,025
Balgay!

680
01:28:47,890 --> 01:28:50,080
I didn't come here to take your life.

681
01:28:55,753 --> 01:28:58,823
Listen to me carefully.

682
01:29:41,925 --> 01:29:45,925
Won't you kill someone who betrayed you?

683
01:29:45,925 --> 01:29:49,925
I want such a mighty commander
like you to have my back.

684
01:29:51,518 --> 01:29:55,518
Yesterdays are over. Let's look ahead now.

685
01:29:58,371 --> 01:30:02,371
Our enemies are the same.
That's why I'm here.

686
01:30:03,591 --> 01:30:04,641
Geyhatu!

687
01:30:09,227 --> 01:30:11,377
What do you want from me, Osman?

688
01:30:11,377 --> 01:30:18,337
If we can agree, you'll give me
Alişar and I'll give you Geyhatu.

689
01:30:26,108 --> 01:30:29,618
Our secret will remain hidden.

690
01:30:35,736 --> 01:30:37,356
Lower your weapons.

691
01:30:41,425 --> 01:30:45,425
Will we fight Geyhatu with
my handful of Nökers?

692
01:30:45,716 --> 01:30:49,716
Remember. I also have a handful of Alps.

693
01:30:54,020 --> 01:30:57,140
Geyhatu is coming here with an army.

694
01:30:57,824 --> 01:31:02,264
How will we destroy a mighty
rock with a handful of sand?

695
01:31:02,802 --> 01:31:08,022
If we become one, Geyhatu will be
the one who is scared.

696
01:31:58,136 --> 01:32:02,136
Melik! You failed.

697
01:32:02,312 --> 01:32:04,842
If I ever catch you...

698
01:32:08,437 --> 01:32:10,007
Oh, Melik!

699
01:32:15,159 --> 01:32:18,419
Alişar Bey! You can't catch Melik.

700
01:32:42,479 --> 01:32:46,479
- Who sent you?
- Balgay did, Dündar Bey.

701
01:32:54,337 --> 01:32:56,337
My Bey. Look.

702
01:32:59,621 --> 01:33:04,691
During Batur Bey's funeral at the Tent,
we went after Osman.

703
01:33:06,098 --> 01:33:10,878
Do you remember Balgay's man
who told us where Osman was?

704
01:33:17,132 --> 01:33:21,132
Balgay found Osman.
He is on Kurt hill.

705
01:33:21,600 --> 01:33:23,210
He called you.

706
01:33:31,785 --> 01:33:35,785
Sencer! Keep your mouth shut.

707
01:33:36,750 --> 01:33:39,260
We have tricks within tricks.

708
01:33:52,683 --> 01:33:57,673
Gündüz couldn't have done this.
This is Osman's job, Alişar Bey!

709
01:33:57,673 --> 01:34:00,323
Look! He tied him to a tree ;
so animals eat him!

710
01:34:00,549 --> 01:34:06,929
How could Osman have done this?
Didn't commander Böke take him to Konya?

711
01:34:09,472 --> 01:34:12,212
There's no one who can do this
other than Osman!

712
01:34:15,402 --> 01:34:19,402
They'd be late to Söğüt if
they fought with Gündüz.

713
01:34:19,669 --> 01:34:22,589
But they got there in time.

714
01:34:23,449 --> 01:34:28,639
Alişar Bey!
I told you to take Osman's life there!

715
01:34:29,305 --> 01:34:35,165
Can't you work out that .
Böke can't deal with Osman?

716
01:34:39,065 --> 01:34:46,945
Dündar Bey!
I lost countless soldiers in this case!

717
01:34:47,441 --> 01:34:50,431
What are you calling me out for?

718
01:34:51,112 --> 01:34:55,672
Don't you remember everything
I've done for you?

719
01:34:57,807 --> 01:35:01,807
I do, Alişar Bey.
I do.

720
01:35:04,384 --> 01:35:12,354
But if Osman is back, I can't imagine
how much blood will be spilt.

721
01:35:12,354 --> 01:35:15,424
You should remember that.

722
01:35:20,764 --> 01:35:27,134
We can't beat Geyhatu's army. But that
doesn't mean we can't kill him.

723
01:35:27,254 --> 01:35:30,694
- How?
- As Genghis Khan said...

724
01:35:30,694 --> 01:35:35,814
If Turks begin to fight, they'll
trap Satan in hell.

725
01:35:37,738 --> 01:35:41,738
- You trust yourself too much.
- I do if you're with me.

726
01:35:43,251 --> 01:35:45,521
Besides, we won't be alone.

727
01:35:45,521 --> 01:35:50,011
Kayıs and all the other
oppressed Tents will be with us.

728
01:35:50,806 --> 01:35:53,456
But Alişar...

729
01:35:54,746 --> 01:35:59,526
There are no issues if our
enemies are the same.

730
01:36:00,612 --> 01:36:03,752
Alişar's poor life doesn't
mean anything to me.

731
01:36:03,752 --> 01:36:08,592
I don't care about Geyhatu or
the wrecked Seljuk throne he's sitting on.

732
01:36:09,207 --> 01:36:11,367
I want liberty in my Tent!

733
01:36:12,262 --> 01:36:16,862
Then we'll go our separate ways.

734
01:36:24,110 --> 01:36:27,470
Geyhatu sent a message
to Alişar with his commander.

735
01:36:28,052 --> 01:36:29,952
We captured it this morning.

736
01:36:31,510 --> 01:36:39,690
He ordered him to kill all the Kayıs and
hang you in the middle of Söğüt.

737
01:36:42,447 --> 01:36:45,237
Many traitors' blood was spilt in Söğüt.

738
01:36:45,680 --> 01:36:49,680
We'll see who hangs who when he
comes to Söğüt.

739
01:36:52,942 --> 01:36:59,782
We're not alone. My commanders and Nökers
are on their way here to end Geyhatu.

740
01:37:00,063 --> 01:37:04,063
They're coming. But don't assume
I forgot about Genghis Khan's laws.

741
01:37:05,472 --> 01:37:11,342
We'll talk about it when the time comes.
First, we'll get you Geyhatu's throne.

742
01:37:11,714 --> 01:37:17,004
And my Tent will get its liberty.
Then you'll get what you want.

743
01:37:24,829 --> 01:37:28,829
How could I not see this until now?

744
01:37:31,294 --> 01:37:34,824
- Are you sure about this, Sencer?
- I am, my Bey.

745
01:37:34,824 --> 01:37:38,824
I still remember how he said,
"Balgay sent me."

746
01:37:43,727 --> 01:37:49,247
Then Alişar Bey is lying to us.

747
01:37:58,622 --> 01:38:01,872
You look bothered. What is it, father?

748
01:38:05,817 --> 01:38:09,817
It's Alişar, son.

749
01:38:11,064 --> 01:38:15,334
I think Alişar Bey has a plan for me.

750
01:38:16,397 --> 01:38:21,897
Do you think he's trying to make a Kayı's
Bey because of his hatred towards Osman?

751
01:38:23,381 --> 01:38:29,271
Politics, father. Why does it matter
when everyone wins?

752
01:38:29,961 --> 01:38:33,401
These storms will stop once you
become a Bey.

753
01:38:34,496 --> 01:38:39,666
They will. But keep your eyes open.

754
01:38:40,724 --> 01:38:44,194
You're his right hand.

755
01:38:47,656 --> 01:38:53,466
I'll hear about every step he takes.

756
01:38:53,466 --> 01:38:55,386
Don't worry, father.

757
01:39:07,367 --> 01:39:09,057
Commander Böke!

758
01:39:18,015 --> 01:39:20,385
Take the horse inside! Go!

759
01:39:21,326 --> 01:39:23,736
- Go.
- Commander Böke!

760
01:39:24,249 --> 01:39:26,609
What happened? Are you okay?

761
01:39:28,370 --> 01:39:31,680
Balgay attacked!

762
01:39:33,065 --> 01:39:34,775
He took Osman.

763
01:39:35,977 --> 01:39:37,777
I hardly escaped.

764
01:39:39,400 --> 01:39:44,210
Both of them are condemned
to stay together to stay alive.

765
01:39:46,162 --> 01:39:54,552
Either Geyhatu will kill all the Kayıs,
or you'll be quick and get your Tent back!

766
01:39:55,269 --> 01:39:57,049
There's no other way!

767
01:39:59,119 --> 01:40:01,929
I know where Balgay and Osman are.

768
01:40:02,997 --> 01:40:07,627
I found out about Osman's nest.
I followed them.

769
01:40:08,946 --> 01:40:13,656
We can wipe them with a sudden ambush!

770
01:40:17,487 --> 01:40:20,277
Tell me, Commander Böke.
Tell me!

771
01:40:23,581 --> 01:40:29,751
Bamsı Bey, what's our situation?
Are the covers at the entrance ready?

772
01:40:30,058 --> 01:40:34,058
They're ready, Gündüz Bey.
The covers are ready.

773
01:40:34,321 --> 01:40:38,321
the quivers are full of arrows.
Swords are sharp.

774
01:40:38,556 --> 01:40:43,586
Even our breaths are ready!

775
01:40:44,051 --> 01:40:45,831
Bless you!

776
01:40:47,838 --> 01:40:53,848
This time our fight is with our own blood.

777
01:40:54,212 --> 01:41:00,662
I know both of you had good times
with my uncle Dündar.

778
01:41:01,583 --> 01:41:04,993
What do your hearts say about this fight?

779
01:41:09,639 --> 01:41:18,619
We went and return such
battlefields as men, thank Allah.

780
01:41:20,055 --> 01:41:23,355
Dündar was with us in some of them.

781
01:41:23,997 --> 01:41:30,047
But our friendship will continue...

782
01:41:31,103 --> 01:41:35,103
... as long as we're on the same path.

783
01:41:37,085 --> 01:41:39,545
For this reason...

784
01:41:39,600 --> 01:41:43,600
... if someone leaves this path...

785
01:41:46,565 --> 01:41:49,245
... it's our duty to hit them
like a ton of bricks.

786
01:41:49,888 --> 01:41:51,808
Remember this.

787
01:41:52,323 --> 01:41:57,103
That's what our hearts say.

788
01:41:57,321 --> 01:42:00,711
- Thank you.
- Our goal...

789
01:42:00,999 --> 01:42:03,299
... is to bring prosperity to Kayı,
Gündüz Bey.

790
01:42:03,710 --> 01:42:08,140
We want nothing more than Allah's sake,
our Tent's peace...

791
01:42:08,140 --> 01:42:10,740
... and our hearts' happiness.

792
01:42:11,186 --> 01:42:16,116
Our blood will boil if it's about
our Tent's future, my Gündüz.

793
01:42:16,116 --> 01:42:21,186
Thank you, Abdurrahman Gazi.
Praise be! Then...

794
01:42:21,186 --> 01:42:25,310
... I'll make your blood boil even more
with a message.

795
01:42:25,839 --> 01:42:28,879
What is it, son? What message is it?

796
01:42:29,697 --> 01:42:32,147
I received a blessed message.

797
01:42:33,522 --> 01:42:36,362
Guys...
We're invited to a wedding.

798
01:42:37,237 --> 01:42:40,107
- What wedding?
- I hope nothing is wrong.

799
01:42:40,712 --> 01:42:43,392
One of Sheikh Edebali's Dervishes came.

800
01:42:45,069 --> 01:42:49,429
Bala Hatun and our Osman Bey will marry.

801
01:42:49,429 --> 01:42:51,539
They're expecting you to come too,
he said.

802
01:42:51,539 --> 01:42:54,849
- How wonderful!
- What are you saying?

803
01:42:55,320 --> 01:42:58,780
What are you saying, my Gündüz?
What are you saying?

804
01:42:58,921 --> 01:43:04,701
- Wonderful! Abdurrahman Gazi!
- How wonderful, Bamsı brother!

805
01:43:04,701 --> 01:43:09,201
My dark-eyes Osman!
My valiant with the looks of an eagle!

806
01:43:11,126 --> 01:43:16,176
My Osman will form his own tent!
Will create his own house!

807
01:43:16,176 --> 01:43:20,246
Just when he was putting his
life out for his Tent...

808
01:43:21,963 --> 01:43:26,193
... he'll bring new lives to Kayı.
New lives!

809
01:43:26,193 --> 01:43:29,803
- May Allah protect him!
- Amen.

810
01:43:29,803 --> 01:43:34,143
May Allah make our Osman live
a long, fortunate life!

811
01:43:34,143 --> 01:43:39,143
How nice of a valiant he become!
Thank Allah.

812
01:43:39,143 --> 01:43:42,513
May Allah give him
dutiful children like himself!

813
01:43:42,541 --> 01:43:45,661
- Allah willing!
- Allah willing, Abdurrahman Gazi!

814
01:43:47,185 --> 01:43:52,165
Come on. It's time to prepare.
Bamsı Bey.

815
01:43:52,888 --> 01:43:55,448
Take the best precautions possible.

816
01:43:56,434 --> 01:44:00,594
Abdurrahman Gazi. Take Alps
to take their positions.

817
01:44:01,376 --> 01:44:03,946
We'll go to the wedding secretly.
No one will know.

818
01:44:03,946 --> 01:44:05,516
Okay, Gündüz Bey.

819
01:44:53,506 --> 01:44:57,506
How wonderful! Let me take a look at you!

820
01:45:01,884 --> 01:45:03,824
It looks wonderful on you.

821
01:45:07,426 --> 01:45:11,426
Praise be my girl.
My beautiful daughter.

822
01:45:20,918 --> 01:45:23,458
I wish my mother Ulduz was with me.

823
01:45:26,228 --> 01:45:28,848
I wish she saw my happiness, Selcan Hatun.

824
01:45:29,328 --> 01:45:34,688
My beautiful daughter.
My Osman is an orphan just like you.

825
01:45:36,295 --> 01:45:41,225
I wish his sons saw this day.

826
01:45:43,306 --> 01:45:47,306
But thankfully I'm here
to see this moment.

827
01:45:50,479 --> 01:45:56,249
Your elders have rights in this moment.

828
01:45:56,668 --> 01:46:02,318
I need to say what they
must have said to you. Come with me.

829
01:46:15,879 --> 01:46:21,109
It's easy to create a home, my daughter.
It's hard to keep it standing.

830
01:46:21,862 --> 01:46:26,732
The wife's troubles are different,
the husband's troubles are different.

831
01:46:27,748 --> 01:46:31,288
The real craft is
to understand those troubles...

832
01:46:31,288 --> 01:46:34,568
... and be a companion to your husband.

833
01:46:36,883 --> 01:46:42,743
If you see a strong household,
know that there is a strong wife in there.

834
01:46:43,371 --> 01:46:47,021
The husband comes after the wife
inside the house.

835
01:46:47,021 --> 01:46:51,741
The female creates the house,
the husband makes it famous.

836
01:46:55,438 --> 01:47:02,148
Protect your home, my beautiful daughter.
Look after your home and your man.

837
01:47:05,800 --> 01:47:11,420
May my almighty Allah bless you
with beautiful children.

838
01:47:12,739 --> 01:47:17,439
And long lives for you
to look after those children.

839
01:47:20,015 --> 01:47:26,455
Don't be upset! You became a friend to
me and a companion for my Osman.

840
01:47:26,849 --> 01:47:29,699
I'm your mother from now on.

841
01:47:34,476 --> 01:47:36,756
Thankfully, Selcan mother.

842
01:47:38,720 --> 01:47:46,170
I'm still too young. Be my guide so you
can correct me when I'm wrong.

843
01:47:46,787 --> 01:47:49,047
Show the path to me when I'm mistaken.

844
01:47:50,121 --> 01:47:51,771
Hopefully.

845
01:47:54,742 --> 01:47:59,372
Bala! There can be no brides
without hennas, my daughter! Let's go.

846
01:48:02,234 --> 01:48:05,544
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(in the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.)

847
01:48:12,155 --> 01:48:14,645
How wonderful!

848
01:49:51,800 --> 01:49:53,250
Commander Böke!

849
01:49:56,192 --> 01:49:57,332
Tell me.

850
01:50:03,418 --> 01:50:05,368
I deceived Alişar.

851
01:50:05,570 --> 01:50:08,840
He' and Dündar Bey will fall into the
trap of Osman Bey.

852
01:50:08,875 --> 01:50:10,525
Really?

853
01:50:10,941 --> 01:50:13,071
It's not that easy.

854
01:50:13,158 --> 01:50:14,458
Why?

855
01:50:15,178 --> 01:50:18,148
Alişar will gather all of his soldiers.

856
01:50:18,553 --> 01:50:20,193
Like a pitched battle? Huh?

857
01:50:21,458 --> 01:50:22,708
Even worse.

858
01:50:23,833 --> 01:50:27,833
We can't cope with them if Balgay's
soldiers don't catch.

859
01:50:28,540 --> 01:50:31,510
Don't worry about these, Commander Böke.

860
01:50:31,571 --> 01:50:34,571
Osman Bey must've known something.

861
01:50:34,945 --> 01:50:38,395
Go to the palace now. They shouldn'
t get suspicious.

862
01:50:46,046 --> 01:50:49,296
Osman bey got you, Alişar.

863
01:51:06,145 --> 01:51:10,145
"I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah...

864
01:51:10,145 --> 01:51:13,665
and I bear witness that Muhammad is
the messenger of Allah" -Shahada.

865
01:51:18,985 --> 01:51:22,625
Bala Hatun, daughter of Sheikh Edebalı...

866
01:51:23,494 --> 01:51:26,274
do you accept to marry
Osman, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi...

867
01:51:26,585 --> 01:51:31,025
in exchange for him giving 200 dram golden...

868
01:51:31,778 --> 01:51:34,828
as a bride price?
- I do.

869
01:51:35,099 --> 01:51:37,599
- Do you accept?
- I do.

870
01:51:37,917 --> 01:51:40,247
- Do you accept?
- I do.

871
01:51:45,039 --> 01:51:47,379
Osman, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi...

872
01:51:47,859 --> 01:51:53,589
do you accept to marry Bala Hatun....

873
01:51:53,679 --> 01:51:57,479
who is the daughter of Sheikh Edebalı?

874
01:51:57,509 --> 01:51:58,339
I do.

875
01:51:59,540 --> 01:52:01,990
- Do you accept?
- I do.

876
01:52:03,212 --> 01:52:05,772
- Do you accept?
- I do.

877
01:52:16,552 --> 01:52:18,702
You as witnesses...

878
01:52:19,005 --> 01:52:22,865
Abdurrahman Ghazi, Zülfikar Dervish...

879
01:52:23,005 --> 01:52:25,325
do you act as a witnesses?

880
01:52:25,365 --> 01:52:27,725
- I do.
- I do.

881
01:52:27,946 --> 01:52:33,436
Then I solemnize your marriage...

882
01:52:33,705 --> 01:52:35,795
in the presence of witnesses here.

883
01:52:39,291 --> 01:52:43,291
May Allah bless your marriage.

884
01:52:43,482 --> 01:52:45,862
- Amin.
- Amin.

885
01:52:47,171 --> 01:52:49,341
Mashaallah, my valiant.

886
01:52:54,356 --> 01:52:57,726
To Allah...

887
01:52:58,040 --> 01:53:01,480
to our Prophet, Mohammad...

888
01:53:01,480 --> 01:53:04,390
may
peace be upon him.

889
01:53:04,553 --> 01:53:07,493
- Amin.
- Amin.

890
01:53:07,583 --> 01:53:11,083
- My Allah, bless this marriage.
- Amin.

891
01:53:11,105 --> 01:53:13,735
Give them respect for each other and...

892
01:53:13,735 --> 01:53:17,175
perseverance for their marriage.
- Amin.

893
01:53:17,232 --> 01:53:21,732
Don't give them hate and dissension.

894
01:53:22,052 --> 01:53:24,242
Amin.

895
01:54:26,500 --> 01:54:30,500
- May Allah bless us.
- Amin.

896
01:54:30,739 --> 01:54:34,739
May Allah make your house...

897
01:54:34,847 --> 01:54:38,427
full of knowledge and wisdom.
- Amin.

898
01:54:39,312 --> 01:54:41,262
I know and believe that...

899
01:54:42,009 --> 01:54:46,389
your marriage isn't just an agreement.

900
01:54:47,014 --> 01:54:51,014
It's a pearl of holy wisdom.

901
01:54:51,289 --> 01:54:55,289
May Allah make you and your descendants...

902
01:54:56,898 --> 01:55:01,848
soldiers for Allah's way.
- Amin.

903
01:55:06,654 --> 01:55:10,654
" Exalted is your Lord, the Lord of
might, above what they describe...

904
01:55:11,217 --> 01:55:13,057
...and peace upon the messengers...

905
01:55:13,524 --> 01:55:18,024
...And praise to Allah, Lord of the
worlds. Al Fatihah. " Surah As- Saffat.

906
01:56:13,525 --> 01:56:24,284
Erlik Khan, make Cenghiz Khan's
soul our leader.

907
01:56:26,739 --> 01:56:31,199
Let our swords
speak, let the death shut up.

908
01:56:32,840 --> 01:56:36,990
Let our swords
speak, let the death shut up.

909
01:56:37,085 --> 01:56:41,085
Let our swords
speak, let the death shut up.

910
01:56:41,215 --> 01:56:44,455
Let our swords
speak, let the death shut up.

911
01:56:44,626 --> 01:56:48,626
Let our swords
speak, let the death shut up.

912
01:56:57,430 --> 01:56:59,940
It's complicated.

913
01:57:00,454 --> 01:57:03,974
Everything became so complicated.

914
01:57:04,289 --> 01:57:07,679
May Allah grant us to
ride out the storm...

915
01:57:08,003 --> 01:57:12,003
and get rid of the burdens, Inshaallah.

916
01:57:12,929 --> 01:57:16,189
Inshaallah, Aygül.
Inshaallah.

917
01:57:22,087 --> 01:57:23,627
Burçin...

918
01:57:24,655 --> 01:57:27,745
What will you wish when
we ride out the storm?

919
01:57:28,148 --> 01:57:32,148
- What do you want to happen?
- What should I?

920
01:57:32,195 --> 01:57:34,805
I want our old order.

921
01:57:35,922 --> 01:57:37,172
No.

922
01:57:39,065 --> 01:57:44,385
I think you think of something else.
You have other wishes.

923
01:57:45,646 --> 01:57:49,966
Your hearts wants someone.
I think you know.

924
01:57:51,769 --> 01:57:55,769
But, pull yourself together.

925
01:57:56,524 --> 01:57:58,544
What are you talking about, mother?

926
01:58:00,749 --> 01:58:02,169
Burçin.

927
01:58:03,522 --> 01:58:05,772
What does your heart want?

928
01:58:11,176 --> 01:58:14,286
You think of Bahadır brother...

929
01:58:14,402 --> 01:58:15,802
No.

930
01:58:17,143 --> 01:58:18,903
Good.

931
01:58:19,564 --> 01:58:22,294
It shouldn't happen.

932
01:58:24,404 --> 01:58:25,854
Look.

933
01:58:25,977 --> 01:58:29,767
You think he is like a mountain but...

934
01:58:29,848 --> 01:58:33,848
mountains are heavy.

935
01:58:34,916 --> 01:58:37,786
Why don't you ever speak of good things?

936
01:58:38,261 --> 01:58:40,681
You always think bad.

937
01:58:41,673 --> 01:58:45,673
Don't you see how much my
Bahadır brother has changed?

938
01:58:45,757 --> 01:58:47,897
Do you see, Aygül?

939
01:58:49,618 --> 01:58:52,028
Don't be sure.

940
01:58:52,304 --> 01:58:57,044
Those eyes have seen much, you know.

941
01:58:58,070 --> 01:59:00,700
A person's nature doesn't change.
Ever.

942
01:59:04,137 --> 01:59:06,817
Bahadır isn't reliable.

943
01:59:07,481 --> 01:59:09,091
You'll wait.

944
01:59:09,766 --> 01:59:11,156
You'll see.

945
01:59:11,599 --> 01:59:13,009
Okay, mother.

946
01:59:13,861 --> 01:59:15,701
You've said enough.

947
01:59:18,194 --> 01:59:19,394
Burçin.

948
01:59:20,753 --> 01:59:24,453
Listen to your heart.

949
01:59:25,267 --> 01:59:27,567
My mother is angry with my brother.

950
01:59:28,397 --> 01:59:32,397
She always thinks of old things.
That's why she's angry.

951
01:59:33,662 --> 01:59:36,402
I trust Bahadır brother.

952
01:59:37,054 --> 01:59:41,054
May Allah grant you the best.

953
01:59:49,799 --> 01:59:51,499
My Bala.

954
02:00:07,487 --> 02:00:09,187
My beginning.

955
02:00:09,940 --> 02:00:13,940
My end. My yesterday, my tomorrow.

956
02:00:14,064 --> 02:00:17,044
My dream, my reality.

957
02:00:17,812 --> 02:00:19,272
And my only wish.

958
02:00:22,048 --> 02:00:26,708
Welcome to my life and heart.

959
02:00:31,191 --> 02:00:32,571
Osman.

960
02:00:35,269 --> 02:00:37,329
I never gave up.

961
02:00:38,497 --> 02:00:42,497
I never gave up on my love.

962
02:00:43,199 --> 02:00:45,649
Your name became my prayer.

963
02:00:46,399 --> 02:00:49,779
My heart was so full of that prayer.

964
02:00:51,721 --> 02:00:55,501
Thank Allah that we came to these days.

965
02:00:55,635 --> 02:01:00,235
From now on, I wish to
close and open my eyes with you.

966
02:01:01,052 --> 02:01:06,332
I wish our Allah treat us with His mercy.

967
02:01:06,572 --> 02:01:09,772
I wish he makes us grow together
and raise.

968
02:01:16,711 --> 02:01:20,081
Believe me, my Bala.
Believe me.

969
02:01:21,748 --> 02:01:24,388
Allah will grant us...

970
02:01:24,662 --> 02:01:30,082
girls and boys who will run in our tent
and maintain our lineage.

971
02:01:30,699 --> 02:01:32,989
Believe it as I do.

972
02:01:33,273 --> 02:01:37,273
Believe it as I believe it.

973
02:01:38,471 --> 02:01:42,021
Our destiny will be good.
Our tent will be good.

974
02:01:42,662 --> 02:01:46,362
Our souls will always be in these lands.

975
02:01:48,608 --> 02:01:52,608
But first we'll kill people...

976
02:01:52,608 --> 02:01:56,098
who are trying to harm our tent.

977
02:01:57,345 --> 02:02:01,345
We'll kill people who want to kill us.

978
02:02:01,748 --> 02:02:03,848
Your way is my way, Osman.

979
02:02:04,646 --> 02:02:09,426
I'll follow you wherever you go.

980
02:02:11,195 --> 02:02:15,195
If you give me duty, I'll deal with it.

981
02:02:16,448 --> 02:02:20,218
- Don't hesitate about me.
- Why should I, my Bala?

982
02:02:20,312 --> 02:02:22,782
You're my reason to praise.

983
02:02:23,763 --> 02:02:25,743
I take my power from my Allah...

984
02:02:26,700 --> 02:02:28,910
and then you.

985
02:02:31,078 --> 02:02:34,248
May Allah grant me to bring Alişar
down a peg...

986
02:02:34,272 --> 02:02:37,692
and kill him...

987
02:02:37,922 --> 02:02:41,682
and then...

988
02:02:41,742 --> 02:02:46,002
make me come back to you.
- Inshaallah.

989
02:02:46,871 --> 02:02:48,461
Inshaallah.

990
02:02:56,339 --> 02:02:57,609
Bala.

991
02:03:27,981 --> 02:03:30,561
Take care of yourself.

992
02:03:33,651 --> 02:03:36,091
Wait for me, Hatun.

993
02:03:39,453 --> 02:03:42,523
I'll wait for you my whole life, Bey.

994
02:03:45,015 --> 02:03:46,915
May Allah help you on your way.

995
02:03:48,634 --> 02:03:52,074
Come and back fast.

996
02:03:53,729 --> 02:03:55,069
Inshaallah.

997
02:05:31,898 --> 02:05:32,828
My Bey...

998
02:05:36,775 --> 02:05:38,075
Take this.

999
02:05:39,053 --> 02:05:41,793
This is Batur brother's dagger.

1000
02:05:42,656 --> 02:05:46,246
This dagger
is entrusted to you like my revenge.

1001
02:05:49,106 --> 02:05:53,106
I know that everything I've
entrusted to you is safe.

1002
02:06:04,488 --> 02:06:10,008
You talk as if you haven't put
off your hijab.

1003
02:06:10,677 --> 02:06:14,317
I don't hold a grudge against Gündüz Ağa
and Bamsı Bey.

1004
02:06:14,504 --> 02:06:16,474
My problem is with Osman.

1005
02:06:17,232 --> 02:06:19,542
There's blood between us.

1006
02:06:20,647 --> 02:06:24,097
I can't keep calm even if I drink
Osman's blood.

1007
02:06:26,781 --> 02:06:28,101
I wish...

1008
02:06:29,270 --> 02:06:34,750
that you'll shed that murderer's
blood with my brother's dagger.

1009
02:06:38,523 --> 02:06:40,303
You wish and...

1010
02:06:41,695 --> 02:06:45,695
I can fill this pool with not
only Osman's blood...

1011
02:06:45,774 --> 02:06:49,774
but also everyone's blood if they're
after Osman.

1012
02:06:49,976 --> 02:06:52,806
Then go and come
back with glory.

1013
02:06:53,020 --> 02:06:55,360
May your sword be sharp.

1014
02:06:56,945 --> 02:07:01,875
Let everyone see who's
controlling this land.

1015
02:07:14,162 --> 02:07:18,162
We went through hoops together.

1016
02:07:18,928 --> 02:07:21,588
We shared happiness.

1017
02:07:25,135 --> 02:07:28,285
You've always prayed for us.

1018
02:07:30,509 --> 02:07:31,819
Now...

1019
02:07:33,636 --> 02:07:37,126
always pray for us, my Sheikh.

1020
02:07:39,771 --> 02:07:40,611
We...

1021
02:07:41,355 --> 02:07:44,845
walk the same way with the same goal.

1022
02:07:46,250 --> 02:07:53,120
Our prayers and support will
always be with you, son.

1023
02:08:02,139 --> 02:08:05,539
My precious ones.

1024
02:08:08,724 --> 02:08:12,724
They're entrusted to Allah and then you.

1025
02:08:16,861 --> 02:08:19,641
Inshaallah, I'll come back
from this war and...

1026
02:08:19,736 --> 02:08:22,866
take my entrustments from you.

1027
02:08:25,179 --> 02:08:28,009
We've entrusted our lives to each other.

1028
02:08:29,104 --> 02:08:31,984
We'll protect them.

1029
02:08:32,401 --> 02:08:34,851
Don't worry, Osman Bey.

1030
02:08:37,255 --> 02:08:38,645
Thanks.

1031
02:08:38,712 --> 02:08:42,712
May my Allah support you, who's
going to the war for freedom...

1032
02:08:42,712 --> 02:08:46,582
with his invisible army.

1033
02:08:48,062 --> 02:08:51,632
Go and come back with prosperity.

1034
02:08:52,061 --> 02:08:55,471
Thank you, my Sheikh.

1035
02:09:03,440 --> 02:09:05,310
Everyone here...

1036
02:09:07,477 --> 02:09:09,147
witness that...

1037
02:09:09,810 --> 02:09:13,150
not even a single one of us is after...

1038
02:09:13,602 --> 02:09:16,372
his own desires.

1039
02:09:20,294 --> 02:09:21,874
Our goal...

1040
02:09:22,255 --> 02:09:26,845
is to bring these lands justice and peace.

1041
02:09:28,945 --> 02:09:30,405
Now...

1042
02:09:31,646 --> 02:09:33,826
give me your blessings.

1043
02:09:33,886 --> 02:09:36,676
- We do.
- Give me your blessings.

1044
02:09:36,699 --> 02:09:41,859
- We do.
- Give me your blessings.

1045
02:09:42,544 --> 02:09:43,774
We do.

1046
02:09:51,178 --> 02:09:52,438
Come on!

1047
02:10:07,760 --> 02:10:11,760
Infidels that stand against us!

1048
02:10:12,087 --> 02:10:16,087
They will find Hamza's courage...

1049
02:10:16,709 --> 02:10:21,859
Yasin's guts, Ammar's tenacity here.

1050
02:10:22,793 --> 02:10:26,203
I swear that our aim is independence...

1051
02:10:26,876 --> 02:10:30,146
our armor is shahada!

1052
02:10:32,317 --> 02:10:37,087
Justice forever!
Independence forever!

1053
02:10:38,075 --> 02:10:42,075
Allah is the greatest!

1054
02:10:43,618 --> 02:10:47,618
Allah is the greatest!

1055
02:10:47,659 --> 02:10:51,659
Allah is the greatest!

1056
02:10:57,547 --> 02:10:59,927
Ey, son.

1057
02:11:00,048 --> 02:11:05,268
Remember, our path is for ever.

1058
02:11:05,569 --> 02:11:08,949
Our aim is to conquer hearts.

1059
02:11:09,274 --> 02:11:12,364
Our case is to be vassal (of Allah)

1060
02:11:14,131 --> 02:11:16,061
Ey, son.

1061
02:11:16,533 --> 02:11:20,533
Be the justice in the shadow of crescent.

1062
02:11:20,844 --> 02:11:23,524
Destroy the cruels.

1063
02:11:23,614 --> 02:11:26,924
Help the oppressed.

1064
02:11:27,285 --> 02:11:32,395
Dominate the wars and be veteran,
be the state!

1065
02:11:32,993 --> 02:11:34,203
Ey son.

1066
02:11:35,045 --> 02:11:37,855
Be Bey to your community.

1067
02:11:38,174 --> 02:11:41,384
Be the conqueror for oppressed ones.

1068
02:11:41,451 --> 02:11:44,691
Be cruel to the cruels.

1069
02:11:45,343 --> 02:11:48,853
Be the peace.

1070
02:11:49,341 --> 02:11:54,131
Be the state of the states!

1071
